        "title": "refactor(codex): split event projector test suite",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Codex event-projector regression suite had grown to 6,865 lines, obscuring ownership boundaries and requiring a grandfathered max-lines exemption.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSplit the monolith into 16 cohesive suites around the projector's assistant, usage, media, echo, terminal, commentary, reasoning, native-event, command, tool, replay, and verbose-hook behaviors. A private shared harness retains the exact setup, cleanup, and fixture behavior, including explicit lifecycle registration for Vitest's shared module cache. The obsolete suppression and baseline entry are removed.\n\nThis is an AI-assisted, maintainer-requested behavior-neutral refactor. I inspected the matching sibling Codex app-server contracts directly: notification wire names in `../codex/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/protocol/common.rs`, notification payloads in `v2/item.rs`, `v2/turn.rs`, and `v2/notification.rs`, and event-to-notification projection in `protocol/event_mapping.rs`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior changes. Maintainers get smaller, ownership-focused regression suites, and the Codex projector no longer needs a max-lines exemption.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs <all 16 event-projector suites>` — 16 files, 168 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/check-changed.mjs -- config/max-lines-baseline.txt <17 split files>` — hosted typecheck, lint, formatting, import-boundary, and max-lines gates passed: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29667792520\n- Direct `oxfmt` and type-aware `oxlint` over the split files — passed.\n- Mechanical suite-body comparison against the original monolith — byte-identical apart from formatter-owned separator whitespace.\n- Per-commit autoreview — no accepted/actionable findings, overall correctness 0.98. The only scanner refusal was the deleted synthetic fixture `OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-1234567890abcdefZZZZ`; the structurally identical sanitized review pair was clean.\n",
